SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Final Notification to Trading Partners about 
 Taking Action Now Before MaineCare’s New Online Portal Goes Live
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Final Notification to Trading Partners about Taking Act
 ion Now Before MaineCare’s New Online Portal Goes Live\nFinal Notificati
 on to Trading Partners about Taking Action Now Before MaineCare’s New On
 line Portal Goes Live\nAug 24\, 2026\nA refreshed and upgraded MIHMS is co
 ming in mid October 2026. The Office of MaineCare Services (OMS)\, in pa
 rtnership with Gainwell Technologies\, is launching an upgraded MIHMS\, to
  bring enhanced security\, improved usability\, and a more modern experie
 nce to better support your day-to-day work.\nThe upgrade will include a ne
 w “MaineCare Partner Portal” that will replace what is known today as 
 the “Health PAS Online Portal.” Please note that\, until the October g
 o-live\, we will continue using the name “Health PAS Online Portal” in
  communications related to current functionality.\nYou can read more about
  the benefits to providers and members on the\nHealth PAS Online Portal\n.
 \nTrading Partners Preparation\nThis is the final notice reminding trad
 ing partners to take action to prepare for the transition to the up
 graded online portal\, called the MaineCare Partner Portal.\nTrading pa
 rtners include providers\, billing agents\, health plans\, clearinghouses\
 , and business associates. Trading partners have an important role to play
  in supporting a smooth transition and uninterrupted access to the portal 
 after go-live.\nPortal Access Impacts and Required Actions Before Go‑Li
 ve\nThe preparation activities and changes below will improve system secur
 ity by ensuring the right people have the right access\, at go-live and on
 going. Most actions are only for Admin (R7) users.\nMost important:\nProv
 iders with duplicate emails need to make changes to their portal user acc
 ounts now to assist with account migration to the upgraded portal. 
 O\nn September 1\, we will terminate current Admin (R7) user accounts that
  share an email address with anothe\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/provid
 ers/provider-bulletins/final-notification-trading-partners-about-taking-ac
 tion-now-mainecares-new-online-portal
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/final-noti
 fication-trading-partners-about-taking-action-now-mainecares-new-online-po
 rtal
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
