SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Upcoming Federal Changes to MaineCare Eligibi
 lity for Some Non-citizens
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Upcoming Federal Changes to MaineCare Eligibility for S
 ome Non-citizens\nUpcoming Federal Changes to MaineCare Eligibility for So
 me Non-citizens\nAug 20\, 2026\nWe are writing to inform you about an upco
 ming change to MaineCare eligibility that may affect some of your MaineCar
 e patients. This change is required by federal legislation signed into law
  in July 2025 (also called H.R.1\, One Big Beautiful\nBill\n\, P.L.119-21\
 , or Working Families Tax Cuts Act) that made changes to the Medicaid prog
 ram nationally. These changes apply in all states\, including Maine.\nBegi
 nning October 1\, 2026\, MaineCare eligibility is changing for some noncit
 izen groups. As a result\,\nsome individuals\nwho currently receive full M
 aineCare benefits will no longer qualify for full coverage and will instea
 d be eligible only for Emergency Services MaineCare. An explanation of cov
 ered benefits under Emergency Services MaineCare is available in the\nMain
 eCare Benefits Manual\n\, Chapter 1\, Section 1.02-4(D).\nThese changes wi
 ll\nnot\naffect children under age 21\, or pregnant individuals through 12
  months after the end of their pregnancy. Please note that the Office for 
 Family Independence (OFI) is still completing the state rulemaking process
  to implement these federal requirements.\nWhat You Should Know:\nThe elig
 ibility changes are expected to take effect on October 1\, 2026.\nMembers 
 who are affected will receive a formal Notice of Decision from OFI before 
 any eligibility changes take place. These notices are expected to be maile
 d in September 2026.\nSome members received an early awareness letter in J
 une or July 2026 to let them know they may be affected. This letter was in
 formational only and is not an eligibility determination.\nHow You Can Hel
 p:\nAs a trusted healthcare provider\, you can play an important role in h
 elping your patients prepare for these changes by:\nEncouraging pati\nhttp
 s://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/upcoming-federal-c
 hanges-mainecare-eligibility-some-non-citizens-2026-08-20
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/upcoming-f
 ederal-changes-mainecare-eligibility-some-non-citizens-2026-08-20
